install Pyinstaller:

Open the cmd window Type: pip install pyinstaller

in the cmd windowd Go to the folder containing your Python code

Type: pyinstaller --onefile nameOfFile.py
Your executable file will go to a "dist" folder in the same directory as your python code

When you run the program, best to run by the cmd window with a command call so as to see error messages.

Add icon images to the folder holding the .exe. The .exe will need to access the image.

to stop the terminal window from opening: python -m PyInstaller --onefile --windowed TKUserGuidedAutomation.py note, it automatically will process all needed dependency files imported
